Step 4 durable probe (delivered worktree at HEAD 2f8daa41057989c7318f18c00b881e788791d4fc before task commit).

Measurement anchors:
- `git grep -n -E '[0-9a-f]{64}' -- 'scripts/release/*.mjs'` -> no matches (exit 1 is the expected empty grep; wrapper reported NO_64_HEX_LITERALS_IN_RELEASE_MJS).
- `pnpm typecheck:release` -> exit 0, executed `$ tsc ... scripts/release/release-subject.mjs ...`.

Full positive probe source (run with `node --experimental-strip-types --input-type=module -e <source>`):
```js
import { execFileSync } from "node:child_process";
import { generateKeyPairSync } from "node:crypto";
import { resolve } from "node:path";
import { deriveContractDigest } from "./packages/control-room-client/src/index.js";
import { GENERATED_CONTRACT_PINS } from "./packages/control-room-client/src/generated/generated-client.js";
import { buildReleaseSubject, RELEASE_COMPONENTS } from "./scripts/release/release-subject.mjs";
const sourceRoot = resolve(".");
const sourceSha = execFileSync("git", ["rev-parse", "HEAD"], { cwd: sourceRoot, encoding: "utf8" }).trim();
const { privateKey } = generateKeyPairSync("ed25519");
const result = buildReleaseSubject({ privateKey, signingKeyId: "task-a9c6d4a5-probe", source: { objectFormat: "sha1", sourceSha }, sourceRoot });
const derived = deriveContractDigest();
const generated = GENERATED_CONTRACT_PINS.contractDigest;
const evidence = { derived, generated, equal: derived === generated, ok: result.ok, componentCount: result.ok ? result.componentCount : null };
console.log(JSON.stringify(evidence));
if (!result.ok || derived !== generated || RELEASE_COMPONENTS.length !== 6 || result.componentCount !== 6) process.exit(1);
```
Exit 0 output:
`{"derived":"a2d053ed83272ecd97f39543d3e1a744b88ae0d0ed4c1c9feee3a126f928b3a1","generated":"a2d053ed83272ecd97f39543d3e1a744b88ae0d0ed4c1c9feee3a126f928b3a1","equal":true,"ok":true,"componentCount":6}`

This proves the production release subject derives the same contract digest carried by the generated client, and the actual release builder accepts the six-component subject.
